\section{Conclusion}\label{section_conclusion}
In this paper, a cascaded online learning flight control system is developed for angle-of-attack tracking. We introduced two techniques to improve action smoothness: online temporal smoothness and low-pass filter. Online temporal smoothness is verified through simulation to effectively reduce the amplitude of virtual pitch rate reference and control surface deflection. The low-pass filter is able to remove the high-frequency signals of pitch rate reference from a frequency domain, which can not be achieved by only using online temporal smoothness technique. Therefore, a \textit{hybrid} approach that combines temporal smoothness and a low-pass filter makes the best benefit of improving action smoothness.



