\subsection{Training Configurations}
In order to implement PASCAL, we adopt the code framework of QCFS ~\cite{bu2023optimal}. We use the Stochastic Gradient Descent optimizer~\citep{bottou2012stochastic} with a momentum parameter of 0.9. The initial learning rate is set to 0.1 for CIFAR-10 and ImageNet, and 0.02 for CIFAR-100. A cosine decay scheduler~\citep{loshchilov2016sgdr} is used to adjust the learning rate. We apply a  $5 \times 10^{-4}$ weight decay for CIFAR datasets while applying a  $1 \times 10^{-4}$ weight decay for ImageNet.


