The captured metrics include execution time and key micro-architectural events, such as ac{LLC} misses, memory access counts, and cycles spent on the system bus. These metrics are vital for evaluating the impact of shared hardware resources—like the \ac{LLC} and memory controllers—on workload performance and predictability.
