\label{exa:hemoglobins}
The PDB contains thousands of hemoglobin structures.
We consider here the structure 2hhb as a standard, and compare it with oxygenated 1hho, which contains an extra oxygen whose transport is facilitated by hemoglobin.
In both cases, we considered the main chains (entity 1, model 1, chain A) of 141 residues. 
Table \ref{tab:haemoglobin_invariants} showed the TRIN and BRI invariants for the first 3 residues of 2hhb and 1hho.
