For instance, the PDB files 1hho and 2hhb in Fig.~\ref{fig:hemoglobins}~(right) include HELX\_P4  consisting of only residues 50 and 51, and HELX\_P5  of length 20 over residue indices $i=52,\dots,71$.
Fig.~\ref{fig:hemoglobins} shows that a `constant' interval of little noise appears only for $i=54,\dots,70$.
Hence new invariants allow a more objective detection of secondary structures,  which will be explored in future work.
