\subsubsection{Estimating damping coefficients}%
\label{sss:estCoeff}

Next, we employ the minimization routine from \Cref{ss:optDamping} to infer the
Rayleigh damping coefficients from data, and use these estimated coefficients
$\alphaStar$ and $\betaStar$ in the construction of the reduced-order damping
matrix.
For this set of experiments, we only consider \soQuadbt{} to highlight the
effects of the estimated coefficients on the reduced model error.
The data $\Bg_{k}$ used to infer the damping coefficients are the evaluations
of the transfer function $\BG(\i \vartheta_{k})$ and $\BG(\i\zeta_{k})$ at the
left and right quadrature points.
For solving the minimization problem~\cref{eqn:rayleighOpt}, we use the
built-in MATLAB optimizer \texttt{fminunc} provided with the
gradients~\cref{eqn:alphaDeriv,eqn:betaDeriv} from \Cref{thm:grads}.
The internal minimization algorithm is the BFGS method with step and optimality
tolerances both set to $10^{-8}$.

