\vspace{-9.0pt}
\subsubsection{Nominal Synthesis}
The next step is to perform finite horizon
nominal synthesis on the scaled plant.  This step is performed using
a special case of the synthesis results described in~\cite{Green1995}. This yields a controller $K^{(i)}$ minimizing the induced norm
from $[\tilde{w}^T, \tilde{d}^T]^T$ to $[\tilde{v}^T, e^T]$.

