% $ J_\text{CPC}(\phi_i, \theta_i)$ の最適化は個別のエージェントで独立に行われる。本研究ではそれぞれのエージェントの離散的なメッセージ$m_i$をone-hot特徴量として表現し、$\vm = (m_i, \dots, m_K)$は$K$体のエージェントのメッセージを結合した$MK$次元のベクトルで表現される。最適化においては、それぞれのエージェント自身のメッセージについては以下のstraight-through gradient estimatorを用いる。
The optimization of \( J_\text{CPC}(\phi_i, \theta_i) \) is performed independently by each individual agent. Practically, each agent’s discrete message \( m_i \) is represented as a one-hot feature vector, and \( \vm = (m_1, \dots, m_N) \) denotes the concatenation of messages from \( N \) agents, forming a vector of dimension \( N \times K \). For optimization, we use the following straight-through gradient estimator \cite{bengio2013estimating} for each agent’s own message:
\begin{eqnarray}
    {\tilde m}_i(x_i) = m_i + \log Q_{\phi_i}(m_i|x_i) - \mathbf{sg}\left[\log Q_{\phi_i}(m_i|x_i) \right]
\end{eqnarray}
% ただし $\mathbf{sg}[\cdot]$は勾配計算を止めるオペレーターである。したがって、$i$番目のエージェントの学習では$\vm(x_i) = (m_1, \dots, {\tilde m}_i(x_i), \dots, m_K)$を入力としてつかって勾配計算を実現する。またKLダイバージェンスも深層強化学習のテクニックを応用したサンプル近似を以下のように導入する\cite{}
Here, \( \mathbf{sg}[\cdot] \) denotes the stop-gradient operator. Accordingly, in the training of agent \( i \), gradients are computed using the input \( \vm(x_i) = (m_1, \dots, \tilde{m}_i(x_i), \dots, m_K) \), where only the agent’s own message is treated as a function of its input and the rest are detached. In addition, the KL divergence is approximated using a sampling-based technique inspired by methods from deep RL \cite{schulman2020apporx}, as follows:
\begin{eqnarray}
    &\KL\left(Q_{\phi_i}(m_i|x_i)\|P(m_i)\right) \approx \left(\kappa - 1\right) - \log \kappa,&\\
    &\kappa = \frac{Q_{\phi_i}(m_i|x_i)}{P(m_i)}.&
\end{eqnarray}

%結果として得られたCPCによるメッセージモジュールの学習はLin et al. \cite{lin2021learning} のオートエンコーダに基づくコミュニケーションモジュールと同様の構成をしているが、メッセージのデコーダーがメッセージ全体$\vm$から復号するモデルになっており、個体ごとの目的関数にKL divergenceが追加されている点が異なる。このとき、KL divergence の項を$\beta$-VAEのように重み付けし、$P_{\theta_i}(x_i|\vm) \triangleq P_{\theta_i}(x_i|_i)$と限定することでLin et al. の手法を記述できるという意味で、我々の方法は先行研究の一般化となっている。また先行研究ではオートエンコーダに基づくメッセージの学習がなぜ有効であるかを説明できてこなかったが、CPCに基づく我々の導出では結合メッセージが状態推定に対応し、これはエージェント同士の観測の情報共有を意味する。
%The CPC-based communication module resembles the method based on auto-encoders proposed by Lin et al.~\cite{lin2021learning}. However our approach differs from previous approach in that the decoder reconstructs from the entire message vector $\vm$, and each agent’s objective function includes an additional KL divergence term. When the KL term is weighted in a manner similar to a $\beta$-VAE \cite{higgins2017beta} with $\beta=0$, and the decoder is restricted as $P_{\theta_i}(x_i|\vm) \triangleq P_{\theta_i}(x_i|m_i)$, the formulation reduces to that of Lin et al., implying that our method constitutes a generalization of their approach. Moreover, while the effectiveness of message learning based on autoencoders was not theoretically justified in prior work, our derivation based on CPC interprets the joint message as corresponding to state estimation, thereby providing a principled account of inter-agent information sharing.
The CPC-based communication module resembles the autoencoder-based method proposed by Lin et al.~\cite{lin2021learning}. However, our approach differs in that the decoder reconstructs from the entire message vector \(\vm\), and each agent’s objective function includes an additional KL divergence term. When the KL term is weighted as in a \(\beta\)-VAE~\cite{higgins2017beta} with \(\beta = 0\), and the decoder is constrained such that \(P_{\theta_i}(x_i \mid \vm) \triangleq P_{\theta_i}(x_i \mid m_i)\), our formulation reduces to that of Lin et al., indicating that our method generalizes their approach. Furthermore, whereas the effectiveness of message learning based on autoencoders was not theoretically justified in prior work, our CPC-based derivation interprets the joint message as supporting state estimation, thus providing a principled account of inter-agent information sharing.


\subsection{MARL-CPC}
% 本研究ではCPCモジュールを用いた情報共有を用いたRLアルゴリズムを提案する。1つめはマルチエージェントのcontextual banditのためのアルゴリズムで、Bandit-CPCと呼ぶ。2つめは状態遷移を含むより複雑な状況に対して適用可能なIPPO-CPCである。
%This study proposes a MARL framework that utilize information sharing via a CPC module, termed MARL-CPC. Based on MARL-CPC, we introduce two algorithms. The first algorithm, called Bandit-CPC, is designed for multi-agent contextual bandit problems. The second, IPPO-CPC, is applicable to more complex scenarios involving state transitions. 

%During the execution of MARL-CPC algorithms, each agent first samples its message \( m_i \) from \( Q_{\phi_i}(m_i \mid x_i) \). The concatenated global message \( \vm \), along with each agent’s hidden representation \( z_i \) obtained by embedding its observation \( x_i \), is then used as input to the subsequent RL modules (Figure~\ref{fig:architecture}). 

This study proposes a MARL framework that facilitates communication learning in MARL via a CPC module, termed \textbf{MARL-CPC}. Based on this framework, we introduce two algorithms. The first, \textbf{Bandit-CPC}, is designed for multi-agent contextual bandit problems. The second, \textbf{IPPO-CPC}, extends the approach to more complex scenarios involving state transitions.

During execution, each agent samples a message \( m_i \) from the variational distribution \( Q_{\phi_i}(m_i \mid x_i) \). The concatenated global message \( \vm \), together with each agent’s hidden representation \( z_i \) obtained by embedding its observation \( x_i \), is then provided as input to the subsequent RL modules (Figure~\ref{fig:architecture}).

The objective function of both algorithms is expressed as the sum of the RL term $J_\text{RL}$ and the CPC term $J_\text{CPC}$. The overall objective function to maximize for agent $i$ of MARL-CPC is expressed as follows:
\begin{eqnarray}
    J(\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i) = \E_t\left[J_\text{RL}(\eta_i) + J_\text{CPC}(\theta_i, \phi_i)\right],
\end{eqnarray}
%ただしここでの期待値演算子$\E_t$は有限のバッチサンプルによるempirical averageを表す。$J_\text{CPC}$は先のセクションで説明したサンプル近似を用いて評価する。
% PPOの最適化においての勾配計算はCPCモジュールには伝搬せず、CPCとPPOの勾配計算はそれぞれ進行する。最終的な全体のPPO-CPCの損失関数は以下で表現される。
%Here, $\eta_i$ is the parameter of agent-$i$'s policy $\pi_i$. The expectation operator \( \mathbb{E}_t \) denotes an empirical average computed over a finite batch of samples. The pseudocode is presented in Algorithm 1. During optimization, gradient computation is not propagated through the CPC module; instead, gradient computations for CPC and RL proceed separately.
Here, \( \eta_i \) denotes the parameters of agent \( i \)'s policy \( \pi_i \). The expectation operator \( \mathbb{E}_t \) represents an empirical average computed over a finite batch of samples. The pseudocode is provided in Algorithm~\ref{alg:marl-cpc}. During RL optimization, gradients are not propagated through the CPC module. Instead, gradient computations for the CPC and RL components are performed independently.

\begin{algorithm}[t]
\caption{MARL-CPC pseudocode}
\begin{algorithmic}[1] % [1] enables line numbering
%\STATE Input: MARL-CPC components $(\pi_i, P_{\theta_i}, Q_{\phi_i}$) and their parameters $(\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i)$ for each agent $i\in\{1, \dots, N\}$, respectively.
\STATE Initialize parameters $(\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i)$ for each agent.
\FOR{$\text{iteration}=0,1,2,\dots$}
    \STATE{Collect sample sets $\{\mathcal{D}_i\}_{i=1,\dots,N}$ in the environment using $\{\pi_i, Q_{\phi_i}\}_{i=1,\dots,N}$}.
    \FOR{$i=0,1,2,\dots,N$}
        \STATE{Make mini-batches $\{\mathcal{D}_i^k\}_{k=0,1,\dots}$ using data $\mathcal{D}_i$}
        \FOR{all mini-matches}
            \STATE{Calculate the RL loss $J_\text{RL}(\eta_i)$ using data $\mathcal{D}_i^k$ and (\ref{eq:loss_bandit}) or (\ref{eq:loss_ppo}).}
         \STATE{Calculate the CPC loss $J_\text{CPC}(\theta_i, \phi_i)$ using data $\mathcal{D}_i^k$ and (\ref{eq:loss_cpc}).}
        \STATE{Update parameters using some gradient ascent: \begin{eqnarray*}
            (\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i)\leftarrow (\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i) + \alpha \nabla_{\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i}J(\eta_i, \theta_i, \phi_i).
        \end{eqnarray*}}
        \ENDFOR
    \ENDFOR
\ENDFOR
\end{algorithmic}
\label{alg:marl-cpc}
\end{algorithm}

\vspace{-3mm}
\subsubsection{Bandit-CPC}
% このアルゴリズムはそれぞれのエージェントにおいて個別の観測と報酬の定義が与えられるcontextual banditにおいて、個々のエージェントの情報共有によって利益を受ける可能性のある環境に対して有効な手法である。このとき、エージェント$i$が1回の試行で得た利得を$r_i$とすると、方策$\pi_i$の改善に使う最大化すべき目的関数は以下となる。
This algorithm is effective in environments where each agent is provided with individually defined observations and rewards in a contextual bandit setting, and where agents can potentially benefit from sharing information with one another. In this context, letting $r_i$ denote the reward obtained by agent $i$ in a single trial, the objective function to be maximized for improving the policy $\pi_i$ is given as follows.
\begin{eqnarray}
    J_\text{RL}(\eta_i) = r_i \log \pi_i(a_i|z_i, \vm)
    \label{eq:loss_bandit}
\end{eqnarray}
% ただしここで、$\eta_i$は方策$\pi_i$のパラメータである。この目的関数とCPCの目的関数の和によってエージェント$i$が最大化する目的関数を与える。
Here, $z_i$ is the internal representation of the encoder $Q(m_i|x_i)$ (Figure~ \ref{fig:architecture}). 

\vspace{-3mm}
\subsubsection{IPPO-CPC}
% Explain the joint loss of IPPO and CPC.
% より一般的な状況でのMARL-CPCを扱うため、本研究ではProximal Policy Optimization (IPPO) の表現学習としてCPCモジュールを追加する。IPPOはオン方策のアクタークリティック型の深層強化学習手法であり、深層ニューラルネットワークで表現された方策$\pi_i$と価値推定器$V_{\pi_i}$を勾配法で最適化する。Independent PPO（IPPO）はPPOのシンプルなマルチエージェント拡張であり、複数のPPOエージェントが独立してそれぞれPPOに基づく行動最適化を実行する。ここでは$i$番目のエージェントの方策と価値推定器のパラメータをまとめて$\eta_i$で表す。実際の実装では$\pi_i$と$V_{\pi_i}$はそれぞれ異なる多層パーセプトロンで定義されている。
%For more complex environments beyond contextual bandit environments, we incorporate a CPC module into Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) \cite{schulman2017proximal} as a representation learning. PPO is an on-policy, actor-critic-based deep RL method that optimizes a policy \( \pi_i \) and a value estimator \( V_{\pi_i} \), both parameterized by deep neural networks, using gradient-based methods \cite{kingma2014adam}. Independent PPO (IPPO) is a simple multi-agent extension of PPO, in which multiple PPO agents independently perform action optimization based on their own PPO updates \cite{de2020independent}. Here, we denote the combined parameters of the policy and value estimator for agent \( i \) as \( \eta_i \). In the actual implementation, \( \pi_i \) and \( V_{\pi_i} \) are each defined by separate multilayer perceptrons (MLP).
For environments beyond contextual bandits, we incorporate the CPC module into Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)~\cite{schulman2017proximal} for representation learning. PPO is an on-policy, actor-critic deep RL method that optimizes a policy \( \pi_i \) and value function \( V_{\pi_i} \), both parameterized by deep neural networks and trained via gradient-based methods~\cite{kingma2014adam}. Independent PPO (IPPO) extends PPO to multi-agent settings, allowing each agent to optimize its policy independently using local updates~\cite{de2020independent}. We denote the combined parameters of agent \( i \)'s policy and value networks as \( \eta_i \). In our implementation, \( \pi_i \) and \( V_{\pi_i} \) are modeled using separate multilayer perceptrons (MLPs).


%エージェントを実行する際にはまずエージェントそれぞれのメッセージ$m_i$を$Q_{\phi_i}(n_i|x_i)$からそれぞれサンプリングする。これらを結合した全体のメッセージ$\vm$と、それぞれのエージェントで$x_i$を埋め込んだ隠れ層の出力$z_i$を用いて、後段のPPOの入力とする。$\pi_\text{old}(a_t|\vx_{i,t}, \vm_t)$をサンプリング時の方策として、$r_t(\eta_i) = \pi_{\eta_i}(a_t|\x_{(i,t)}, \vm_t)$とすると、PPOは以下の損失関数の最小化で表される。
Let \( \pi_\text{old} \) denote the policy at the time of sampling, and define \( r_t(\eta_i) = \frac{\pi_i(a_t|z_{i,t}, \vm_t)}{\pi_\text{old}(a_t|z_{i,t}, \vm_t)} \). The subscript \( z_{i,t} \) denotes the internal representation of agent \( i \)'s encoder $Q(m_i|x_i)$ at time step \( t \). The PPO objective is expressed as the minimization of the following loss function:
\begin{eqnarray}
    J_\text{RL}(\eta_i) &=& J_\pi(\eta_i) - c_1 J_V(\eta_i) + c_2 H_\pi(\eta_i) \label{eq:loss_ppo}\\
    J_\pi(\eta_i) &=& \min \Bigl( r_t(\eta_i)A_{i, t} , \text{clip}\left(r_t(\eta_i), 1-\epsilon, 1+\epsilon)A_{i, t} \right) \Bigr)\\
    J_V(\eta_i) &=& \left(V_{\pi_i}(z_{i, t}, \vm_t) - V_{i, t}^\text{targ}\right)^2
\end{eqnarray}
%ただし$\cdot_{i,t}は$i$番目のエージェントの時刻$t$で得られた値を表す記法である。$ $A_{i, t}$はサンプリング時の価値推定器を用いて、generalized advantage estimationで与えられ\cite{}、$H_\pi$は方策のエントロピーを表す。$c_1$, $c_2$, $\epsilon$はそれぞれ正の定数を表し、$\text{clip(\cdot, 1-\epsilon, 1+\epsilon)}$は入力を値域$[1-\epsilon, 1+\epsilon]$内に収める関数である\cite{}。$V_t^\text{targ}$は長さ$T$の軌道のサンプルで得られたempirical return $V_t^\text{targ} = r_t + \gamma r_{t+1} + \gamma^{T-t} V_{\pi_i}(s_T)$である。
Here, the advantage \( A_{i,t} \) is computed using the value estimator at sampling time, based on generalized advantage estimation \cite{Schulmanetal_ICLR2016}. \( H_\pi \) denotes the entropy of the policy. \( c_1=0.5 \), \( c_2=0.01 \), and \( \epsilon=0.2 \) are all positive constants. The function \( \text{clip}(\cdot, 1 - \epsilon, 1 + \epsilon) \) restricts its input to the range \( [1 - \epsilon, 1 + \epsilon] \) \cite{schulman2017proximal}. The target value \( V_t^\text{targ} \) is the empirical return computed from a trajectory of length \( T \), defined as $V_t^\text{targ} = r_t + \gamma r_{t+1} + \cdots + \gamma^{T - t} V_{\pi_i}(z_{i,T}, \vm_T)$.

