This experiment serves as a proof of concept for information sharing established through CPC. It is conducted in a non-cooperative setting where information sharing via communication is beneficial for each individual agent (Figure~\ref{fig:r_bandit}). The environment consists of two agents (Agent-A and Agent-B), each acting independently. In this environment, each agent makes a single decision per episode, and receives an individual reward based on the environmental state and their chosen action.

The single episode is defined by the following rules. The environment possesses a true state $s$, which can be either LEFT or RIGHT, each occurring with a probability of 0.5. Among the two agents, only one is given access to the true state of the environment as part of its observation. Each agent's observation is represented as a two-dimensional binary vector. If an agent $i \in \{0, 1\}$ is informed of the true state, then it receives $x_i = [1, 0]^\top$ when $s = \text{LEFT}$ and $x_i = [0, 1]^\top$ when $s = \text{RIGHT}$. The uninformed agent receives an observation $x_i = [0, 0]^\top$, which provides no information about the true state. Each agent chooses an action $a_i \in \{\text{LEFT}, \text{RIGHT}\}$. If the chosen action matches the true state, i.e., $a_i = s$, the agent receives a reward of $+1$. Otherwise, it receives $-0.1$.

This environment is not cooperative, as the agent that knows the true state can maximize its own reward by learning to match its action to the state, i.e., $a_i = s$, without relying on assistance from the other agent. Consequently, in this setting, the informed agent has no incentive to communicate the state information to the other agent. As a result, reinforcement through rewards alone does not lead to the emergence of communication between agents. However, for the uninformed agent, knowing the true state is clearly advantageous. Without knowledge of the true state, the agent lacks any basis for selecting an appropriate action, reducing its success to chance level. Therefore, if both agents are able to share information about the true state via messages, the total group reward can be increased. Communication with this property has the potential to be established solely through CPC. 

