Let agents engage in game-play using nonstationary policy $\pi^{\lambda}$, where for epoch $k$, agents play $\pi^{k}$, a NE-policy for Lagrangian game $\ccalG(\lambda_k)$. Consider the following set 
\begin{align} \label{eq_Dk1}
\ccalD^{k}_{i}:=\{\lambda\in \mbR^{m}_{+}|d_i(\lambda,\pi^{k}_{-i})-d_i(\lambda^{+},\pi^{k}_{-i})\leq \eta B^2/2 \}    
\end{align}
Here $\lambda^{+}\in \mbR^{m}_{+}$ is some reference lambda which has finite norm, and $k$ is an arbitrary fixed epoch number.   
