\section{Conclusions}
% v1
\if 0
In this paper, we investigated quantization in TTS and proposed a new convolutional layer called BitConv b1.58 to reduce model size. Experimental results applying the proposed method to TTS show that using ternary values weights (-1, 0, 1) does not significantly degrade synthesized speech compared to the conventional QAT method. By storing weight indices instead of the weights themselves, the proposed method achieves a greater reduction in model size than applying QAT to the convolutional layers.
\fi

% v2
