Furthermore, Fig. \ref{fig:robust-cifar} presents the generalization errors of both attack-free DSGD and Byzantine-resilient DSGD with different robust aggregation rules when $\beta=1$. The results depict that the presence of Byzantine agents enlarges the generalization error. These findings are also consistent with observations from the softmax aggregation task on MINIST dataset and align with our theoretical results.




