\section{Introduction}

We adopted GPT-Researcher as the main framework for our LiveRAG submission to use an abstractive summarization paradigm to support answer generation. This approach was one of the best performing systems in TREC NeuCLIR's report generation tasks~\cite{neuclir2024}.
We used Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\footnote{https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct}~\cite{qwen2025qwen25technicalreport} with 8 bit quantization for query formulation.
We used a ColBERT-based search engine~\cite{ecir2022colbert-x} for retrieval with a PLAID-X model trained multilingually~\cite{ecir2024translate-distill}. The retrieval system returned top-ranked passages. Passages were then chunked into snippets. 
Passage snippets were filtered based on the cosine similarity between the original question and the snippet using m2-bert-80M-8k-retrieval\footnote{https://huggingface.co/togethercomputer/m2-bert-80M-8k-retrieval}~\cite{fu2023monarch}. The general architecture appears in Figure~\ref{fig:design}.
Finally, Falcon3-10B-Instruct\footnote{https://huggingface.co/tiiuae/Falcon3-10B-Instruct}~\cite{Falcon3} was used to generate the final response. The remainder of the paper outlines the detailed architecture of our system as well the prompts we used in the different steps in our pipeline. We describe the steps we took to validate the approach and optimize the performance to be able to perform at the required speed for the competition.


\section{System Design}

Our RAG system divided the process into two main stages. In the first stage research was conducted to identify relevant information and in the second stage the response was written. Conducting research included generating queries based on an initial search and then gathering all the responsive data together from the retrieved passages.
Writing the response used the gathered context to generate the final output of the system. In Section~\ref{sec:research} we describe the process for conducting research. Section~\ref{sec:write}
describes the process of generating the response given the research.

