\section{Methods}
In this study, we utilized a mixed-methods approach to thoroughly investigate how students use and perceive GenAI in academic settings. Our methodology integrates quantitative surveys with qualitative focus group discussions to provide both statistical rigor and rich, contextual insights. The quantitative component involves administering pre- and post-intervention surveys across multiple courses and semesters, allowing us to track changes in both usage patterns and attitudes toward GenAI. We then complement this data with in-depth focus groups, which capture nuanced reflections and experiences that surveys alone might overlook. The focus groups are further enriched by happening several weeks after the post-surveys are administered, allowing for an evaluation of the more permanent effect the intervention had.

This section details our overall methodological framework, including survey design, data collection strategies, statistical analyses, and qualitative procedures. By employing paired sample tests and effect size estimations for our quantitative data, and thematic analysis for our qualitative findings, we ensure a comprehensive evaluation of the intervention’s impact on student learning.


