Based on \Cref{fig:compared_to_before_all_combined}, one can see that each course had a different average perceived shift in their desire to use GenAI. Explicitly, CP, DSA-CS, and ENGR skewed towards more usage, while DSA-DSAI skewed towards less usage.  Based on student interactions and focus groups, we hypothesize that DSA-DSAI, as DS/AI majors, were likely to be overreliant on GenAI coming into the intervention, due to their specific major structure and the perceived difficulty of their classes. On the other hand, CS and ENGR majors were more cautious to begin with, erring on the side of under-use, whereas we wanted to encourage all students to use these tools for their educational benefit.

Future studies are necessary to better analyze differences between courses, as this study was primarily designed to measure the overall impact and success of the AI-Lab intervention on CS undergraduates.



